The data files in data/ are derived data, with these terms:

- Britain and Ireland grids, places and river tables (data/page/uk_a.png,
  data/page/uk_b.png, data/page/page.json "uk" part, data/page/places.json "uk"
  part, data/uk_*.csv) contain OS data (c) Crown copyright and database right
  2026 (OS Open Rivers, OS Open Names), used under the Open Government Licence
  v3.0, and heights from AWS Terrain Tiles (Mapzen/Tilezen, from SRTM, EU-DEM and
  other open sources listed at
  https://github.com/tilezen/joerd/blob/master/docs/attribution.md). They are
  released under the Open Government Licence v3.0 with these attributions.

- World grids and tables (data/page/world_idx.png, data/page/world_sea.png,
  data/page/page.json "world" part, data/world_*.csv) are derived from
  HydroBASINS and its pour points, which are subject to the HydroSHEDS version 1
  licence agreement (https://www.hydrosheds.org). Required attribution:
  This product (Where Rain Goes) incorporates data from the HydroSHEDS version 1
  database which is (c) World Wildlife Fund, Inc. (2006-2022) and has been used
  herein under license. WWF has not evaluated the data as altered and
  incorporated within Where Rain Goes, and therefore gives no warranty regarding
  its accuracy, completeness, currency or suitability for any particular
  purpose. Portions of the HydroSHEDS v1 database incorporate data which are the
  intellectual property rights of (c) USGS (2006-2008), NASA (2000-2005), ESRI
  (1992-1998), CIAT (2004-2006), UNEP-WCMC (1993), WWF (2004), Commonwealth of
  Australia (2007), and Her Royal Majesty and the British Crown and are used
  under license. The HydroSHEDS v1 database and more information are available at
  https://www.hydrosheds.org.
  Users of these files must follow the HydroSHEDS licence terms, including this
  attribution.

- Sea areas: Flanders Marine Institute (2018) IHO Sea Areas, version 3,
  https://www.marineregions.org (CC BY 4.0). River, lake, land and country data:
  Natural Earth (public domain). Cities: GeoNames (CC BY 4.0;
  data/world_cities.csv, data/page/places.json "world" part).
